pages
mapFunctionsPage
	^HelpTopic
		title: '4] Map Functions Squeak Maps' "has to be updated manually"
		icon: (HelpIcons iconNamed: #mapPinIcon)
		contents: 'MAP FUNCTIONS
-------------

Scroll:
Place the cursor in the map area and hold left-click to pan the map.

Zoom:
Place the cursor in the map area and scroll to zoom.

Search:
Search for a location by typing its name in the field in the top left corner.

Manage Categories:
On the left side of the application the white box shows your pin-categories. 
Below you have the option to add and remove categories and thereby personalize 
the map.

Set Pins:
Double-click on your chosen location in the map area (or search for the 
location). A pin will appear.

Save/Categorize Pins:
Set a pin and then click on Save Pin. Save the pin to one of your categories.
By clicking on your categories, all the respective pins will appear on the map.

Routing:
To be able to route you need to connect to an API.
- In the lower left corner click on Select API and choose one of those 
  available (recommended: OpenStreetMaps).
- Next to the Select API button is an API Key button, where you need to add 
  an API key for the API you selected.
- You have to generate an API key via the website of the respective API 
  (note that some APIs are not free to use).

To route:
- First, search for a location in the search area
- Then click on Directions
- A new interface opens that allows you to enter a Start and Destination, 
  and select a preferred mode of transportation (walk, bike, car) -- 
  click Go to route
- To close the routing interface, click the x (close) button in the upper 
  right corner of the left sidebar'